      <div type="clause">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVAtr">IV Atr</ref></head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">[De institutis Lundoniae; et primum: quae portae observabantur. [2.] De teloneo dando ad Bilingesgate. [3.] De teloneo retento [4.] De hamsocna vel in porto vel in via regia. [5.] De falsariis et eis consentientibus. Et de cum falsa moneta deprensis. [6.] Et de monetariis.] [In M, Hk, Br of Q]</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">[Concerning the decrees of London; and first: what gates were manned. [2] Concerning the paying of tax at Billingsgate. [3] Concerning withheld tax [4] Concerning breaking and entering either in the harbour or on the king's highway. [5] Concerning false coiners and those who assist them. And about issuing false currency. [6] And concerning the coinage.]</ab>
      </div>
